{
  "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
  "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner (United States ex rel. Polansky)",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The government lacks the statutory authority to dismiss a False Claims Act case after declining to proceed with the action, and that conclusion follows directly from the Act's plain text, structure, history, and purpose."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 9,
        "start": 9
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But things can change, as the other side points out. The discovery could reveal new facts. There could be a new administration that comes in. There could be burdens on the agency that were not apparent at the outset."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 24,
        "start": 24
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAGAN: Well, it says the court shouldn't limit the status and rights. That's a different thing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Mr. Geyser, perhaps you've said everything that you have to say on this point, but just to be clear, what do you think -- if the government intervenes belatedly, what do you think it can do that would not constitute a limitation of the debtor's status and rights?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Gorsuch",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0001-0004",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GORSUCH: Mr. Geyser, let -- let -- let's -- I just want to give you an opportunity to discuss the standard. Suppose we disagree with you and we think the government can intervene at this stage and seek to dismiss the case. There's a hearing that's called for under (c)(2)(A). What's that supposed to look like in your view?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Barrett",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BARRETT: It sounds more like intermediate scrutiny really."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0001-0006",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 38,
        "start": 38
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Mr. Geyser, assuming, as did Justice Gorsuch, that I believe the government can intervene and can dismiss, to dismiss, because I think that's a form of proceeding with the action. You can take discovery. You can make a motion for summary judgment. You can do all sorts of things, including moving to dismiss. So assume I do that."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Jackson",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0002-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE JACKSON: So do we have legislative history that just explains the changes that you're talking about? Do we know why they struck those things?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: But does it have to do more -- does the government have to do more than simply say those things?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Government",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0003-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. LIU: -- in a sort of shocks the conscience way. But we do think the hearing serves two important purposes."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 69,
        "start": 69
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So let's talk about political pressure. There's no reason related to the case. It's simply that the senator of this defendant's home state doesn't want this defendant to be sued."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
      "confidence": 0.93,
      "document_hash": "6b6e8792b1c2fe78c42676b0c931d8c11a642746d4ad85def34c7f6fbc902b14",
      "evidence_id": "ev-6b6e8792b1c2-0004-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 90,
        "start": 90
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE ALITO: Yeah. So the -- so the government should foot the whole bill, right, should pay the -- the relator and the defendant?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Source extraction",
      "case_id": "2022-21-1052",
